commit 6141f959486b453e3f168667684b9d2fca2399bf
Author: bunnykong <[redacted-email]>
Date:   Sat Oct 10 05:06:46 2026 +0800

    Keep the receiver's type for reload and lock!
    
    Fixes #721. #536 classified reload as the shared runtime's Base return,
    and #671 copied that classification into lock!, so a model method called
    on either result stopped resolving.
    
    Register both methods with the model's own type. Ruby-family emission
    adds concrete forwarders that call the inherited operation and answer
    self, keeping the emitted RBS promise true when Spinel loads the runtime's
    Base declarations. Preserve source overrides and leave the save!/destroy
    return classifications alone.
    
    Cover both method chains, direct returns, identity and refreshed attributes
    on emitted Ruby and native Spinel with RBS seeds. Replace reload's old
    Base-return expectation with receiver-return coverage; retain the save!,
    destroy and destroy! regressions.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <[redacted-email]>

